      "writtenOn": "2026-09-09T15:08:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it make sense to introduce a `meta.requeue` section for these fields?\n\nThey are transport/requeue metadata rather than part of the event payload itself.\n\nNesting them would keep the top-level schema cleaner and leave meta extensible for other metadata categories in the future.\n\nIf we do this, we could also drop the explicit `requeued` boolean.\n\n```\n{\n  \"type\": \"...\",\n  \"instanceId\": \"...\",\n  \"eventCreatedOn\": 123,\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requeue\": {\n      \"retryCount\": 2,\n      \"requeuedOn\": 123456789,\n      \"requeuedByInstanceId\": \"instance-a\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n\nWe would also make sure that when `meta` it is not defined it doesn\u0027t get serialized.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 37
      },
